<title>JAPAN: Japan buys 160,000 tonnes wheat, 40,000 T barley.</title>
<headline>Japan buys 160,000 tonnes wheat, 40,000 T barley.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-03-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Japanese Food Agency said on Thursday it had bought 80,000 tonnes of U.S. wheat, 40,000 of Canadian wheat, 20,000 tonnes of Australian wheat and 20,000 of Australian barley at its weekly tender, all for May shipment.</p>
<p>The agency also said it had bought 20,000 tonnes of U.S. wheat and 20,000 of Canadian barley for April shipment.</p>
<p>Details of the tender results details are as follows, in tonnes.</p>
<p>- MAY SHIPMENT -</p>
<p>WHEAT</p>
<p> U.S.	 80,000	   Western white	    20,000</p>
<p>				   Dark northern spring   40,000</p>
<p>				   Hard red winter</p>
<p>				     (13 percent protein) 20,000</p>
<p> Canada     40,000	   1 Canadian western red spring</p>
<p>								  40,000</p>
<p> Australia  20,000	   Standard white	   20,000</p>
<p>BARLEY</p>
<p> Australia  20,000	   Food			 20,000</p>
<p>- APRIL SHIPMENT -</p>
<p>WHEAT</p>
<p> U.S.	 20,000	   Dark northern spring   10,000</p>
<p>				   Feed wheat		 10,000</p>
<p>BARLEY</p>
<p> Canada     20,000	   Food			 10,000</p>
<p>				   Feed			 10,000</p>
<p>-- Tokyo Commodities Desk (+81-3-3432-7391)</p>
</text>
